<title>GERMANY: Hundt takes over as German employers' group head.</title>
<headline>Hundt takes over as German employers' group head.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dieter Hundt, president of the employers' association of Baden-Wuerttemberg, on Thursday took over leadership of the German federal employer association (BDA) from Klaus Murmann, who has led the BDA for 10 years.</p>
<p>Hundt was elected Murmann's successor in March.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
